  "id": "social-phobia",
  "term": "social phobia",
  "definition": "Social phobia is an anxiety disorder marked by strong fear in social or performance settings where a person expects close attention or judgment from other people. Entering these situations brings on anxiety, and adults usually understand that the fear is out of proportion.",
